    "html": "<h1>Software Architecture<\/h1>\n<p>My lecture notes, simple explanations, and runnable examples for Software Architecture.<\/p>\n<h2>Topics<\/h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n  <th>Topic<\/th>\n  <th>What is inside?<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c2_Architecture_Documentation/README.md\">Architecture Documentation<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Stakeholders, concerns, views, viewpoints, documentation planning, and UML.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c2_1_4_1_View_Model/README.md\">4+1 View Model<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Five perspectives and the worked Catabase example from Week 2.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c3_MVC_and_Design_Patterns/README.md\">MVC and Design Patterns<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Model\u2013View\u2013Controller, execution flow, and when design patterns help.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c4_Architectural_Styles/README.md\">Architectural Styles<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>System organization, architectural tradeoffs, Client\u2013Server, tiers, P2P, components, objects, and SOA.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c6_Design_Pattern/README.md\">Design Pattern<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Creational, structural, and behavioral design patterns, with Python examples.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#c5_Cloud_Database/README.md\">Cloud Database<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Eight study topics covering cloud hosting, SQL/NoSQL, scaling, ACID, Redis, and SQL CRUD.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n  <td><a href=\"#code_example/README.md\">Coding Examples in Class<\/a><\/td>\n  <td>Class coding exercises organized by week.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>Other course topics can be added beside Design Pattern as we study them.<\/p>\n<h2>Running the design-pattern examples<\/h2>\n<p>In VS Code's terminal, first enter the topic folder:<\/p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">cd c6_Design_Pattern\n<\/code><\/pre>\n<p>Then use the commands in the lesson READMEs. Those commands assume the terminal is inside <strong>Design Pattern<\/strong>.<\/p>\n",
    "text": "# Software Architecture\n\nMy lecture notes, simple explanations, and runnable examples for Software Architecture.\n\n## Topics\n\n| Topic | What is inside? |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Architecture Documentation](c2_Architecture_Documentation/README.md) | Stakeholders, concerns, views, viewpoints, documentation planning, and UML. |\n| [4+1 View Model](c2_1_4_1_View_Model/README.md) | Five perspectives and the worked Catabase example from Week 2. |\n| [MVC and Design Patterns](c3_MVC_and_Design_Patterns/README.md) | Model\u2013View\u2013Controller, execution flow, and when design patterns help. |\n| [Architectural Styles](c4_Architectural_Styles/README.md) | System organization, architectural tradeoffs, Client\u2013Server, tiers, P2P, components, objects, and SOA. |\n| [Design Pattern](c6_Design_Pattern/README.md) | Creational, structural, and behavioral design patterns, with Python examples. |\n| [Cloud Database](c5_Cloud_Database/README.md) | Eight study topics covering cloud hosting, SQL/NoSQL, scaling, ACID, Redis, and SQL CRUD. |\n| [Coding Examples in Class](code_example/README.md) | Class coding exercises organized by week. |\n\nOther course topics can be added beside Design Pattern as we study them.\n\n## Running the design-pattern examples\n\nIn VS Code's terminal, first enter the topic folder:\n\n```powershell\ncd c6_Design_Pattern\n```\n\nThen use the commands in the lesson READMEs. Those commands assume the terminal is inside **Design Pattern**.\n"
