    "html": "<pre><code>&quot;&quot;&quot;Class adapter: inherit from the old class instead of holding its object.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n\n# Reuse the same target, old printer, and client as the object-adapter example.\nfrom example import LegacyPrinter, Printer, print_report\n\n\nclass ClassPrinterAdapter(LegacyPrinter, Printer):\n    def print_document(self, text):\n        # print_text() is inherited from LegacyPrinter.\n        self.print_text(text)\n\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    printer = ClassPrinterAdapter()\n    print_report(printer)\n<\/code><\/pre>",
    "text": "\"\"\"Class adapter: inherit from the old class instead of holding its object.\"\"\"\n\n# Reuse the same target, old printer, and client as the object-adapter example.\nfrom example import LegacyPrinter, Printer, print_report\n\n\nclass ClassPrinterAdapter(LegacyPrinter, Printer):\n    def print_document(self, text):\n        # print_text() is inherited from LegacyPrinter.\n        self.print_text(text)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    printer = ClassPrinterAdapter()\n    print_report(printer)\n"
